      answer_en: "Operations synthesis in 30 seconds:\n\nThe factory operates at 72% of its 15,000-unit daily capacity — 10,800 actual units. Three bottlenecks block scale-up toward the 90% target of 13,500 units.\n\nThe €5M investment unlocks 2,700 additional units per day. With a contribution margin of €50 per unit and 250 working days, the annual gain exceeds €33M — a theoretical payback under 3 months.\n\nKey risk: reaching 90% requires addressing the three bottlenecks in the correct sequence to avoid creating a fourth downstream constraint.\n\nRecommendation: approve the investment in two tranches — start with the highest-impact bottleneck, measure actual results before funding the next tranche. Targets: 85% within 6 months, 90% within 12 months.\n\nNext milestone: map the three bottlenecks by impact and resolution timeline before prioritizing the €5M allocation."
